Package: dash
Type: Package
Title: Depth-Aware Structural-Zero and Hellinger Test for Microbiome Differential Abundance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    c(
        person("Yiqian", "Zhang", email = "zhang.16383@osu.edu",
               role = c("aut", "cre")),
        person("Zihan", "Zhu", email = "zihan.zhu@yale.edu",
               role = "aut")
    )
Description: A two-part differential abundance test for microbiome count data.
    DASH combines a structural-prevalence score test, derived from a
    per-taxon structural-zero mixture model with a left-censored normal
    observation component, with a weighted abundance test on Hellinger-Riemann
    intrinsic coordinates (HRIC). The abundance component uses auxiliary
    posterior-presence weights, a censoring-correction nuisance covariate, an
    HC3 sandwich standard error, and a robust affine bias correction. The two
    arms are combined per taxon by a Bonferroni min-P rule and by a Cauchy rule.
